6. Programmable Therapeutics as Control Inputs

The intervention u_t is not restricted to RNA sequence:

u_t = (s_t, \mathcal{L}_t, \rho_t, \tau_t),

where s_t is the therapeutic molecular program, \mathcal{L}_t is the delivery architecture, \rho_t is the dose, and \tau_t is the timing.

For RNA therapeutics,

s_t \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{RNA}}, \qquad \mathcal{L}_t \in \mathcal{L}_{\text{delivery}}.

Thus,

\text{Therapeutic program} = \text{payload} + \text{delivery} + \text{dose} + \text{time}.

This formulation makes explicit that the therapeutic object is a policy over a product space of sequence, delivery, dose, and schedule. Table 1 summarizes a control-theoretic taxonomy for RNA controllers.

