7. Delivery as a Coupled Dynamical System

Delivery is not a static parameter. It is a coupled dynamical system with its own pharmacokinetics, biodistribution, protein corona dynamics, endosomal escape, and immunogenicity.

We introduce a separate delivery state z_t:

z_{t+1} = g(z_t, \mathcal{L}_t, \eta_t),

where \mathcal{L}_t is the delivery architecture and \eta_t represents delivery stochasticity.

The biological response then depends on the effective cytosolic payload availability:

x_{t+1} = f\big(x_t, s_t \cdot h(z_t), \theta, w_t\big),

where h(z_t) maps delivery state to effective intracellular therapeutic activity.

This formulation explains why delivery co-design is difficult. The overall optimization is bilevel:

\min_{\mathcal{L} \in \mathcal{L}_{\text{delivery}}} \mathcal{J}_{\text{outer}}(\mathcal{L}),

subject to

\mathcal{J}_{\text{outer}}(\mathcal{L})
=
\min_{s,\rho,\tau} D\big(F(x,z), x^*\big) + \lambda C(u),

where D measures deviation from the desired state and C is a cost function.

The outer loop over \mathcal{L} is slow and manufacturing-constrained. The inner loop over s,\rho,\tau is faster and more programmable. Programmable lipid nanoparticles provide concrete control handles: corona engineering can detarget the liver and retarget other tissues, SORT lipids enable organ-selective delivery, and barcoded LNP libraries permit empirical identification of the mapping from delivery composition to cell-type tropism.

A concrete relaxation replaces the intractable continuous bilevel problem with a hierarchical procedure. The outer loop selects from a library of N_{\mathcal{L}} validated LNP formulations, typically 10 \le N_{\mathcal{L}} \le 50. The inner loop solves a robust model-predictive control problem over sequence, dose, and schedule, given delivery uncertainty bounds derived from the selected formulation’s empirical biodistribution profile. For N_{\mathcal{L}} \le 50 and a horizon H \le 10, this is tractable via branch-and-bound or warm-started inner solves. The outer loop is updated only when new LNP platforms complete GMP validation, which occurs on timescales of months to years.

