11. The Adaptive Therapeutic Loop

The complete architecture is a closed loop. The patient or biological system is observed through sensing, which feeds state estimation, which updates the patient digital twin, which informs the virtual cell and tissue model, which drives AI therapeutic design, which is constrained by a predictive safety filter, which authorizes a programmable intervention, which acts on the biological system, whose response is measured, and the cycle repeats.

Adaptive Programmable Therapeutics is explicitly a computational-molecular closed loop. The sensor is multi-omic profiling and imaging; the processor is AI state estimation and model-predictive control; the actuator is programmable RNA plus lipid nanoparticle delivery. The loop operates on hours-to-days timescales between doses, unlike implantable closed-loop devices that operate on milliseconds to minutes.

